Template: pi2000web/title
Type: title
Description: Pi-2000Web installation

Template: pi2000web/setup-requested
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Run explicit account setup
 Internal flag used to preserve setup choices between debconf invocations.

Template: pi2000web/admin-password
Type: password
Description: Password for the Pi-2000Web administrator:
 For a new installation, choose a password containing 12 to 1024 characters.
 When running setup on an existing installation, enter its current admin password.
 The same initial password will be used for its MariaDB account.

Template: pi2000web/admin-password-confirm
Type: password
Description: Enter the administrator password again:
 Repeat the password to confirm it before the new accounts are created.

Template: pi2000web/password-error
Type: error
Description: The passwords must match and contain 12 to 1024 characters
 Please enter and confirm the administrator password again.

Template: pi2000web/local-mode
Type: select
Choices: Existing account, Create account with sudo, Disabled
Default: Existing account
Description: Linux account for the owner's Local Terminal:
 Existing account preserves its password and permissions. Creating an account
 makes a separate Linux login with password-required sudo. Other web users
 receive no Linux account or sudo permissions.

Template: pi2000web/local-user
Type: string
Description: Linux username for Local Terminal:
 Enter an existing regular Linux username, or the new username to create.
 Service accounts and root cannot be used. An existing account is never overwritten.

Template: pi2000web/local-port
Type: string
Default: 22
Description: Local SSH server port:
 Local Terminal connects to 127.0.0.1 on this port. Existing SSH settings are preserved.

Template: pi2000web/linux-password
Type: password
Description: Password for the new Linux account:
 Choose a separate password containing 12 to 1024 characters.
 This password is needed for SSH login and sudo. It is not saved in Pi-2000.

Template: pi2000web/linux-password-confirm
Type: password
Description: Enter the Linux account password again:
 Repeat the new Linux account password before the account is created.
